  "status_text": "And here is a table where the NOT gate does pay. While 418 graphs were answering that one NOT gate saves them nothing, Lean checked a different small case the other way. For one four-by-four table, with one row and one column selected and gates reading at most two wires, the least circuit of AND and OR gates has exactly 9 gates (L-meta-6304). With NOT gates allowed, 7 suffice (L-meta-19107), and at 17:48 UTC Lean accepted that 6 cannot (L-meta-29738). So negation saves exactly two gates on this table. Where a NOT gate helps and where it does not is the line this part of the search is drawing.",
